{"evidence":{"id":"E3","kind":"fact","text":"sga for fiscal year ending 2012-12-31 = $670.6M (XBRL tag SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense)","source":"10-K accession 0001336917-13-000011, filed 2013-02-25"},"origins":{"queries":[{"sql":"SELECT * FROM veritas_pg.facts WHERE cik = 1336917 ORDER BY fy_end, CASE concept WHEN 'revenue' THEN 0 WHEN 'cogs' THEN 1 WHEN 'sga' THEN 2 WHEN 'depreciation' THEN 3 WHEN 'net_income' THEN 4 WHEN 'cfo' THEN 5 WHEN 'receivables' THEN 6 WHEN 'current_assets' THEN 7 WHEN 'ppe' THEN 8 WHEN 'assets' THEN 9 WHEN 'current_liabilities' THEN 10 WHEN 'lt_debt' THEN 11 ELSE 99 END","rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2012-12-31","concept":"sga","tag":"SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense","value":"670602000","accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25"}],"mode":"zetaris","label":"executed on Zetaris","table":"facts"}],"rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2012-12-31","concept":"sga","tag":"SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense","value":"670602000","accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2013-12-31","activeRevision":"7d3e957400e5","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25","cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1336917/000133691713000011/0001336917-13-000011-index.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":1,"findingIndex":2,"management_says":"SG&A increased $201M due to higher marketing, selling costs (direct-to-consumer expansion), product innovation/supply chain, and corporate services.","numbers_show":"SG&A rose from $670.6M to $871.6M (E3, E15). Operating cash flow dropped from $199.8M to $120.1M (E6, E18) while net income rose $33.5M. The large cash outflows for selling ($63.9M increase, E40) and marketing ($41.1M increase, E39) directly reduce CFO, and the receivables increase of $34.5M (E7, E19) also consumed cash. The pattern fits the described investment in growth.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E3","E6","E15","E18","E39","E40","E41","E42"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":2,"management_says":"No explicit explanation provided in the evidence pack for the decline in operating cash flow from $199.8M to $120.1M while net income rose from $128.8M to $162.3M.","numbers_show":"CFO fell $79.7M (39.9%) despite a $33.5M rise in net income. SG&A increased $201M (largely cash expenses: marketing +$41M, selling +$64M, product innovation +$51M, corporate +$45M). Current assets rose $225M (receivables +$34.5M, implying inventory +~$190M), current liabilities rose $174M, so net working capital increased ~$50M. The direct-to-consumer expansion cited for revenue growth entails higher cash operating expenses and inventory investment, which would reduce CFO.","fit":"unverified","evidence":["E5","E6","E17","E18","E26","E3","E15","E39","E40","E41","E42","E8","E20","E11","E23"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":1,"rulingIndex":2,"finding_index":2,"ruling":"fits","reason":"SG&A rose $201M (E3, E15) with MD&A breakdown: marketing +$41.1M (E39), selling +$63.9M (E40), product innovation/supply chain +$50.7M (E41), corporate services +$45.3M (E42). CFO fell $79.7M (E6, E18) while net income rose; receivables increased $34.5M (E7, E19). The cash outflows for SG&A and receivables build directly explain CFO decline.","evidence":["E3","E6","E15","E18","E39","E40","E41","E42"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":2,"innocent_explanation":"The $201M SG&A increase reflects cash outflows for marketing, selling, and supply chain to support DTC expansion, which directly reduces operating cash flow alongside receivables growth.","evidence":["E3","E6","E15","E18","E39","E40","E41","E42"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.78}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":2,"finding_index":2,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management provided no explicit explanation for the $79.7M decline in operating cash flow despite higher net income. The defender's explanation (higher cash SG&A and inventory investment) is plausible but not management's stated explanation. The numbers show SG&A increased $201M and current assets increased $225M (receivables +$34.5M, implying inventory +~$190M), but the causal link to direct-to-consumer expansion is not explicitly stated in the MD&A.","evidence":["E5","E6","E17","E18","E26","E3","E15","E39","E40","E41","E42","E8","E20","E11","E23"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":2,"innocent_explanation":"The $79.7M decline in operating cash flow despite higher net income reflects a $201M increase in cash SG&A expenses (marketing +$41M, selling +$64M, product innovation +$51M, corporate +$45M) and a ~$190M increase in inventory and other current assets (current assets rose $225M while receivables rose only $34.5M) to support 18 new retail stores and ecommerce growth, partially offset by a $174M rise in current liabilities.","evidence":["E5","E6","E17","E18","E3","E15","E39","E40","E41","E42","E8","E20","E7","E19","E11","E23"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}}],"audit":[{"seq":3,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E3 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":30,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E30 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":31,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":32,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e95